[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Approach [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhere should the login be recorded?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mB: Server in /login (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mContract says /login records the login; client keeps userId in a session module.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m A: Client POST /events
     [38;5;246mClient sends a separate tracking event after login; reusable event channel.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: A with globals
     [38;5;246mSame as A but window globals instead of ES modules; no load change, harder to test.[39m
